.TH "KOSH\-SWITCHING" "5" "" "kosh" "Koshka Manual"
.SH NAME
kosh\-switching \- migrate an interactive shell environment and login
shell from Bash to Koshka[cite: 1]
.PP
2026\-10\-28[cite: 1]
.PP
Prerequisites \- An installed \f[CR]kosh\f[R] binary, an active Bash
session, and a familiarity with kosh(1) invocation and kosh(5)
configuration[cite: 1].
.PP
Koshka is a command shell that controls execution behavior and startup
file loading through operational modes called moods[cite: 1].
The default \f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood validates shell syntax prior to
execution and rejects scripts containing errors[cite: 1].
The \f[CR]bash\f[R] mood provides Bash compatibility for startup
configurations and legacy scripts[cite: 1].
Keep the current Bash session open in a separate terminal window while
testing startup files to prevent terminal lockout[cite: 1].
.SH CORE PRIMITIVES
.PP
