.SH LOAD EXISTING BASH STARTUP FILES IN KOSHKA
Launch an interactive Koshka session with both the \f[CR]kosh\f[R] and
\f[CR]bash\f[R] startup moods to retain existing Bash aliases,
functions, and environment variables[cite: 1].
.IP
.EX
kosh \-L kosh,bash
.EE
.PP
When \f[CR]\-L kosh,bash\f[R] is passed, Koshka executes the
\f[CR]kosh\f[R] startup sequence first and the \f[CR]bash\f[R] startup
sequence second[cite: 1].
.PP
